		309 -> 314;
	3904 [label="But you are trying to distract me ! While I am not opposed, it is far too soon for such things, n'est pas ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		3904 -> 3905;
	318 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		318 -> 326;
	317 [label="Faith by any name I find beauty in. Tell me, is it new ? Old ? Would I recognize it at all ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		317 -> 324;
		317 -> 325;
	316 [label="You do ! Oh, comme c'est fascinant ! To think someone holds the faith so far into the future, cela remplit mon cœur de joie. I am overwhelmed with joy. Though I think your time in the past may have had something to do with it, no ? Ah, no matter.",shape=box,color=blue];
		316 -> 323;
	315 [label="I respect your response. But I must ask, how are you so certain ? Is that not a kind of faith in itself ? And what is this... Indifférence of yours, if not a god ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		315 -> 320;
		315 -> 321;
		315 -> 322;
	314 [label="+10 Chemistry",color=orange];
		314 -> 319;
	3905 [label="I... would still like an answer to my question, s'il vous plait, if you do not mind. Though now you have me blushing !",shape=box,color=blue];
		3905 -> 308;
		3905 -> 307;
		3905 -> 306;
		3905 -> 305;
		3905 -> 304;
	326 [label="Ah, oui. A wanderer, that is in your name. You have seen many cultures, many faiths, many worlds. Cela est très spirituel, non ? Collected parts of them like seashells.",shape=box,color=blue];
		326 -> 336;
		326 -> 337;
	324 [label="I don't think you'd recognize it at all, no.",shape=box,color=red];
		324 -> 334;
	325 [label="You might recognize parts of it. But other parts would be totally foreign to you.",shape=box,color=red];
		325 -> 335;
	323 [label="I wonder, are you devout to one or the other ? Or do you seek the balance ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		323 -> 331;
		323 -> 332;
		323 -> 333;
	320 [label="I'm not perfectly certain I'm right, no one can be. But I still don't personally believe in gods.",shape=box,color=red];
		320 -> 328;
	321 [label="I think religion exists to fill a hole in people's lives left by the fear of death and the unknown.",shape=box,color=red];
		321 -> 329;
	322 [label="I don't know what the Indifference is, but it isn't a god. We just need to get to the bottom of it. ",shape=box,color=red];
		322 -> 330;
	319 [label="Aah, perhaps the wisest answer of them all! For who are we mere mortals - if we can still claim to be such - to pretend to draw out the design of the Gods ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		319 -> 327;
	336 [label="I think there is also something older, truer, and deeper that speaks to us all. A connective tissue, kind of.",shape=box,color=red];
		336 -> 347;
	337 [label="Exactly. I see something beautiful in all of them, I don't know as anyone has it right or wrong.",shape=box,color=red];
		337 -> 347;
