	384 [label="Ô joie ! I do so much love to learn. I have often wondered if the Luminaries did not wear other faces. Other names.",shape=box,color=blue];
		384 -> 398;
	385 [label="I suppose that might be a surprise, to find someone who wears the cloth to not be strict in their expectations of others. I find preaching to those who are not seeking solace does not win much love.",shape=box,color=blue];
		385 -> 399;
	382 [label="I simply wonder, does our faith bring you peace ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		382 -> 394;
		382 -> 395;
		382 -> 396;
	383 [label="That is a rare gift... and one I hope you wield. To linger at the crossroads too long is to be consumed by strife, I fear.",shape=box,color=blue];
		383 -> 397;
	376 [label="It must be a simpler life, then. To not live by the rules of gods and churches. I admit I am a little jealous.",shape=box,color=blue];
		376 -> 389;
	377 [label="Then I am jealous of you, wanderer ! To live so many centuries, devoid of the need to know the gods.",shape=box,color=blue];
		377 -> 389;
	378 [label="You sound like a disciple of Lua, and I mean that with no offense. Oui, the Crone comes for us all, and weeps her silver tears. But your words make me wonder...",shape=box,color=blue];
		378 -> 390;
	379 [label="Oui, it makes me wonder. I look upon you, the child, the devil, even Monsieur Loid, or le Cardinal... so many centuries stretch behind you all.",shape=box,color=blue];
		379 -> 391;
	380 [label="What kind of dangerous game?",shape=box,color=red];
		380 -> 392;
	381 [label="He doesn't think the Man in the Wall is real, either?",shape=box,color=red];
		381 -> 393;
	374 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		374 -> 387;
	375 [label="I am smiling at your wisdom and kindness towards the beliefs of others.",shape=box,color=blue];
		375 -> 388;
	394 [label="It doesn't.",shape=box,color=red];
		394 -> 400;
	395 [label="I honestly don't think much about it.",shape=box,color=red];
		395 -> 401;
	396 [label="It does.",shape=box,color=red];
		396 -> 402;
	398 [label="They have been known to change their forms to please their followers in other sects. But that is my faith, not yours. I will not preach to those who are not seeking for solace. I find it does not win much love.",shape=box,color=blue];
		398 -> 399;
	399 [label="No, my faith is mine, and yours is your own. I simply hope it brings you peace ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		399 -> 394;
		399 -> 395;
		399 -> 396;
	397 [label="In the end, all must choose a path to walk. But the crossroads is where we must all begin, the balance is the foundation of all structures.",shape=box,color=blue];
		397 -> 403;
	389 [label="But, I wonder... does this not believing, does it bring you peace ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		389 -> 394;
		389 -> 395;
		389 -> 396;
	390 [label="Of whom do you speak of, when you say \"it should\" come for you all ? I look upon you, the child, the devil, even Monsieur Loid, or le Cardinal... so many centuries stretch behind you all.",shape=box,color=blue];
		390 -> 391;
	391 [label="I wonder how many centuries stretch before us now, before Lua will come for us. And I wonder how eagerly I will embrace her when that day should come. But that is my faith, not yours.",shape=box,color=blue];
		391 -> 389;
	392 [label="I do not know just yet. He keeps his schemes to himself like a good devil. But he believes in no gods. Save, perhaps, himself.",shape=box,color=blue];
		392 -> 389;
	393 [label="Non, he does not. He is much like you, he believes in no gods. Save, perhaps, himself.",shape=box,color=blue];
